# Files that define how an agent must BEHAVE — not merely what the code does.
#
# An agent's rules reach it exactly once: CLAUDE.md is injected when its session
# starts, AGENT.md is read in its first minutes, skills load on demand. Nothing
# re-reads them. So an agent that has been working for hours is still operating
# under the rules as they were when it started — and `develop` may have changed
# them underneath it.
#
# `wt merge` refuses to land a branch whose author never saw a change to any
# path below. `bb wt ack` prints the diff (so the new rules actually enter the
# agent's context) and records that it has been seen.
#
# This is an EXPLICIT list, not a heuristic over the diff. Guessing "is this a
# rule, or just a doc?" is precisely how a rule change slips past unnoticed.
# One path or prefix per line; blank lines and #-comments ignored.

CLAUDE.md
dev/wtq/AGENT.md
dev/wtq/README.md
dev/wtq/GOVERNANCE
.claude/skills/
.claude/hooks/
.claude/settings.json
